{
  "slug": "hiss-taxonomy",
  "title": "HISS invariant taxonomy",
  "alt": "Twenty-one HISS invariants structured across deterministic execution, memory safety, governance, and operations families.",
  "text": [
    "Deterministic Execution: HISS-01 (Acyclic DAG Control Flow), HISS-02 (Bounded Loops & I/O Timeouts), HISS-03 (Zero Frame Malloc), HISS-04 (Complexity & Sizing Bounds), HISS-05 (Variable Scoping), HISS-06 (Bounded Concurrency).",
    "Memory & Error Integrity: HISS-07 (Checked Errors & Zero Unwrap), HISS-08 (Static Determinism & Banned Funcs), HISS-09 (Mandatory // SAFETY: Proofs), HISS-10 (5-Layer Zero-Warnings Cascade).",
    "Contracts & Fleet Governance: HISS-11 (Hermetic Supply Chain), HISS-12 (Secret Leak Prevention), HISS-13 (Monotonic Debt Ratchet), HISS-14 (Append-Only ABI & Migration), HISS-15 (3D Test Discipline), HISS-16 (Canonical AGENTS.md & Server Gates).",
    "Agent Operations & Evidence: HISS-17 (State Ledger Discipline), HISS-18 (Diff-Aware CI Efficiency), HISS-19 (Reuse Before Writing), HISS-20 (Replayable Enforcement Evidence), HISS-21 (Platform Neutrality).",
    "Deterministic Execution → Memory & Error Integrity → Contracts & Fleet Governance → Agent Operations & Evidence.",
    "The 21 invariants of the High-Integrity Systems Standard form four governing families from static determinism to agent operations."
